SOUND TEST. Each line says what you should hear, then plays it.

[S1] BEEP: One short, high beep.
@wait 1200
@sound beep
@wait 700
[S2] BOOT: One short PC power-on beep.
@wait 1200
@sound boot
@wait 700
[S3] ERROR: A low, buzzy error tone.
@wait 1200
@sound error
@wait 700
[S4] ALERT: Two quick two-tone chirps.
@wait 1200
@sound alert
@wait 700
[S5] CHIRP: One fast upward chirp.
@wait 1200
@sound chirp
@wait 700
[S6] TICK: A single tiny tick (listen closely).
@wait 1200
@sound tick
@wait 700
[S7] KEYS: A burst of keyboard clicks.
@wait 1200
@sound keys
@wait 700
[S8] SUCCESS: Four rising notes.
@wait 1200
@sound success
@wait 700
[S9] FAIL: Three falling notes.
@wait 1200
@sound fail
@wait 700
[S10] ALARM: A siren rising and falling three times (about 2 seconds).
@wait 1200
@sound alarm
@wait 700
[S11] KLAXON: Three low, harsh pulses (about 2 seconds).
@wait 1200
@sound klaxon
@wait 700
[S12] STATIC: A burst of radio static.
@wait 1200
@sound static
@wait 700
[S13] GLITCH: Digital crackle.
@wait 1200
@sound glitch
@wait 700
[S14] POWERUP: A tone sweeping upward (1 second).
@wait 1200
@sound powerup
@wait 700
[S15] POWERDOWN: A tone sweeping down to a low growl (1 second).
@wait 1200
@sound powerdown
@wait 700
[S16] DIALTONE: A phone dial tone (1.5 seconds).
@wait 1200
@sound dialtone
@wait 700
[S17] RING: A phone ringing twice.
@wait 1200
@sound ring
@wait 700
[S18] BUSY: A busy signal: three beeps (2.5 seconds).
@wait 1200
@sound busy
@wait 700
[S19] DIAL 5550714: Seven touch-tone digits being dialed.
@wait 1200
@sound dial 5550714
@wait 700
[S20] MODEM: A dial-up modem connecting (about 3 seconds).
@wait 1200
@sound modem
@wait 700
[S21] MISSPELLED SOUND: nothing should play. (With Run now, a [TEST] note appears instead.)
@wait 1200
@sound alarmm
@wait 700

Sound test finished. If you heard nothing at all, check your volume and type SOUND ON.

VOICE TEST.

[V1] A robotic voice reads this line aloud while it types out.
@wait 1200
@speak Hello. I am the terminal. Can you hear me?
@wait 300
[V2] A longer line. The script waits for the voice to finish before going on.
@wait 1200
@speak This sentence is a little longer, so you can judge whether the voice is clear enough for players to follow.
@wait 300
[V3] For comparison: the same kind of line with @slow, typed out with no voice.
@wait 1200
@slow This one is silent. Same color, no voice.
@wait 300

Voice test finished. Type SOUND OFF and run VOICE again: the text should still type out, silently. Then type SOUND ON.

SCREEN EFFECTS TEST.
These lines are here so the glitch has something to scramble.
The quick brown fox jumps over the lazy dog.

[E1] FLASH: the screen flashes white once.
@wait 1200
@flash
@wait 700
[E2] FLASH RED: the screen flashes red once.
@wait 1200
@flash red
@wait 700
[E3] SHAKE: the text shakes for half a second.
@wait 1200
@shake
@wait 700
[E4] LONG SHAKE: the text shakes for 2 seconds.
@wait 1200
@shake 2000
@wait 700
[E5] GLITCH: the screen jitters and the last lines scramble for under a second, then go back to normal.
@wait 1200
@glitch
@wait 700
[E6] LONG GLITCH: the same for 3 seconds. Every line should come back exactly as it was.
@wait 1200
@glitch 3000
@wait 700
[E7] EVERYTHING AT ONCE: alarm, red flash, shake and glitch, like a real emergency.
@wait 1200
@sound alarm
@flash red
@shake 800
@sound static
@glitch 1200
@wait 700

Effects test finished.

